INT. NIGHT AQUARIUM - SHARK TUNNEL - NIGHT

A glass tunnel curves through blue-lit water. Sand tiger sharks glide overhead. Footsteps echo on the acrylic.

ROSARIO (30s, wetsuit under a janitor's coverall) walks backward down the tunnel, camera drone in hand. KEZIA (20s, scuba gear half-zipped) follows with a rolling case. ODDVAR (50s, silver beard, pearl earring) stops to stare up at the sharks. PRAKASH (30s, headset, laptop on a strap) types as he walks.

ROSARIO
Check in.

PRAKASH
Cameras are looped. Door's mine.

KEZIA
Case is cold. Heart is not.

Oddvar says nothing. A shark passes. He taps the glass. It turns its head.

ROSARIO
(to the group)
Eyes front. Nobody chats with the fish.

ODDVAR
(murmur, to the shark)
You've got your orders. I've got mine.

At the tunnel's midpoint, a pedestal holds a glass case. Inside, a pearl the size of a plum. Rosario sets down the drone and peels off the coverall, revealing wetsuit. Kezia pops the case, hands her a regulator. Prakash backs up to a pillar and types faster. Oddvar crouches by the pedestal and runs a thumb over its latch, a faint smile on his face, while the sharks wheel closer in a slow ring.

An ALARM chirps. Everyone stills.

PRAKASH
(whisper)
That's not mine.

ROSARIO
Whose is it?

ODDVAR
Mine.

He stands. The pearl is already in his pocket. He walks away, calm, unhurried, past the others. Rosario lunges for his sleeve, misses, and follows him. Kezia drops the case and runs after them both. Prakash stays frozen with the laptop clutched to his chest.

PRAKASH
(to himself)
Of course. Of course it's him.

Overhead, a shark thumps the glass.
